      en: "Jingdezhen, in Jiangxi province, has been the epicenter of Chinese porcelain production for over 1,700 years. Known as the 'Porcelain Capital,' it supplied imperial ceramics during the Ming and Qing dynasties. Today, the ceramics industry remains the city's economic backbone, with numerous factories producing both traditional handmade porcelain and modern industrial ceramics. The city is home to the Jingdezhen Ceramics Institute, a leading research and education center. Exports reach over 100 countries, and the city attracts tourists eager to see ancient kilns and contemporary workshops. In 2014, Jingdezhen was named a UNESCO Creative City of Crafts and Folk Art.",
